  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Where a mistake stops the Host",
      "items": [
        "A declaration's own mistake throws while the Host is composed.",
        "A composition check fails Build(): one InvalidOperationException, one line per problem; container validation throws an AggregateException.",
        "A Kit option out of range fails StartAsync with an OptionsValidationException.",
        "A startup check fails StartAsync before any hosted service starts, so the Host serves and delivers nothing; StartingAsync first fails a Host whose composition checks never ran.",
        "A queue that does not store what it receives fails StartAsync once Wolverine has started."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Wolverine's configuration order",
      "items": [
        "While the Host is composed: UsePouryaKitWolverine's own settings, then the Host's configure.",
        "When Wolverine's options are built: the Kit's routes, handlers, retry policy, delayed-command queues, durability mode, inbox stale time and RabbitMQ topology."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Migrations",
      "items": [
        "The Host applies no Module migrations when it starts.",
        "Wolverine creates its message store tables as it starts, in a Host with a message store.",
        "HostFixture applies every Module's migrations, then starts the Host: in tests only."
      ]
    }
  ]
